T=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat would be the image of the triangle shown above under the action of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that for any linear transformation $T$ with associated $2\\times 2$ matrix $T,$ we have one of the following three possibilities:\n\n- If $T$ is non-singular, i.e., $det(T)\\ne 0,$ then the image of a two-dimensional object is a two-dimensional object. In particular, the image of a polygon with $n$ vertices is a polygon with $n$ vertices.\n\n- If $T$ is singular, i.e., $det(T)=0,$ we have two additional subcases:\n\n- If $T$ has at least one nonzero entry, then the image of a two-dimensional object is a one-dimensional line segment.\n\n- If $T$ is the zero matrix, then the image of a two-dimensional object is the point $(0,0),$ the origin of the coordinate system.\n\nSince $T$ is the zero matrix, the image of our object under the action of $T$ is the origin."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106472 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7d1252e9-f2ac-5adf-9cf5-ef48e35fb747" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Image of an Object Formed by a Singular Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aa5e3475-705f-5e07-a5df-5e5f30b47be7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1351/Source/Images/q-96873-a-4.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186105342} {:answer/id #uuid "aacc0592-89fa-52a0-81dd-48065c4b6f9e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1351/Source/Images/q-96873-a-5.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186105343} {:answer/id #uuid "afd277bf-e8b4-5e67-9d77-55f526df47de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1351/Source/Images/q-96873-a-1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186105344} {:answer/id #uuid "de2919ea-f3fb-55b3-aff8-b42cfbf3a8ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/ho